{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788468778949,"sessionID":"ses_f96f44813ffeMjSGBHDZ7e2mUe","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_07581a91667f4cee82832615","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"gh issue view 149"},"output":"title:\tImplement Float (IEEE binary64 per ADR 0007) across the backends\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t149\n--\nBuild the Float type end to end, per docs/adr/0007-float-is-javascripts-double.md: IEEE 754\nbinary64, matching JavaScript's number representation, no alternative width, no decimal type.\n\nSemantics per gh:145 (the Q37 ruling): admit NaN/Infinity, division by zero returns Infinity\n(IEEE), matching IEEE 754. Division is a total function on Float; Int and Float division have\ndifferent failure behavior (Int still raises on zero divisor).\n\nNot yet settled, needs a call during implementation: exact float literal printing so all seven\nbackends agree byte for byte (default float formatting differs across languages) -- pick a\nformat and hold every backend to it. See draft.md Q37 in plans/questions.md for the fuller\nquestion shape if it still exists, otherwise use the ADR and gh:145 as the source of truth.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Float literals parse and type-check\n- arithmetic (+ - * /) and comparisons work across all seven backends with agreeing output\n- NaN/Infinity are producible and print identically across backends\n- division by zero on Float returns Infinity, not an error (contrast with Int)\n- corpus test coverage added for the above\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","metadata":{"output":"title:\tImplement Float (IEEE binary64 per ADR 0007) across the backends\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t149\n--\nBuild the Float type end to end, per docs/adr/0007-float-is-javascripts-double.md: IEEE 754\nbinary64, matching JavaScript's number representation, no alternative width, no decimal type.\n\nSemantics per gh:145 (the Q37 ruling): admit NaN/Infinity, division by zero returns Infinity\n(IEEE), matching IEEE 754. Division is a total function on Float; Int and Float division have\ndifferent failure behavior (Int still raises on zero divisor).\n\nNot yet settled, needs a call during implementation: exact float literal printing so all seven\nbackends agree byte for byte (default float formatting differs across languages) -- pick a\nformat and hold every backend to it. See draft.md Q37 in plans/questions.md for the fuller\nquestion shape if it still exists, otherwise use the ADR and gh:145 as the source of truth.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Float literals parse and type-check\n- arithmetic (+ - * /) and comparisons work across all seven backends with agreeing output\n- NaN/Infinity are producible and print identically across backends\n- division by zero on Float returns Infinity, not an error (contrast with Int)\n- corpus test coverage added for the above\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"gh issue view 149","time":{"start":1788468778945,"end":1788468778947}},"id":"prt_0690bd4c40010Z0AOtU518aWxq","sessionID":"ses_f96f44813ffeMjSGBHDZ7e2mUe","messageID":"msg_0690bca4a001luJwkSsNPMiqeJ"}}
