{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788468790613,"sessionID":"ses_f96f44813ffeMjSGBHDZ7e2mUe","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_76120b62fd0745768398f650","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git show origin/main:plans/board.yaml | grep -n \"float\" | head -30"},"output":"87:- id: float-format-research\n89:  title: 'Escalation ruling (lane-escalations-168-149 round, float-build-149-siblings-stall, option A): float-build-go/python/rust stalled 6 cumulative runs across 3 lanes, zero commits, before any research. float-build (JS reference) is already landed. Survey how Go (strconv.FormatFloat/ParseFloat), Python (repr(float)/float(str)), and Rust (Display/Debug impls, str::parse) each format an IEEE binary64 float to a string and back versus the JS reference, focusing on round-trip precision and hex/exponent edge cases. The float-build-python lane (~/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python) has an uncommitted diff plus scratch probe files (f64_probe, float_check.py, hexdump.py, paren_probe.py) from a real struggle with this -- read them for a concrete lead, do not modify that lane. Write concrete per-backend formatting guidance (with short verified code snippets) to plans/, so the three build lanes are not rediscovering the same snag on redispatch.'\n95:- id: float-build-rust\n97:  title: Implement Float (IEEE binary64 per ADR 0007) for the Rust backend only, following float-build's JS implementation as the reference. One backend, one commit.\n99:  needs: [float-build, float-format-research]\n102:- id: float-build-python\n104:  title: Implement Float (IEEE binary64 per ADR 0007) for the Python backend only, following float-build's JS implementation as the reference. One backend, one commit.\n106:  needs: [float-build, float-format-research]\n109:- id: float-build-go\n111:  title: Implement Float (IEEE binary64 per ADR 0007) for the Go backend only, following float-build's JS implementation as the reference. One backend, one commit.\