re/toylang-lanes/issue-float-format-research/scratch_float_py.py","text":"import math, struct\n\nvals = [\n    0.0, -0.0, 1.0, -1.0, 0.5, 0.1, 0.2, 0.3,\n    100.0, 1000000.0, 1000000000000.0,\n    1e15, 1e16, 1e17, 1e20, 1e21, 1e22, 1e23, 1e100, 1e300,\n    1e-4, 1e-5, 1e-6, 1e-7, 1e-8, 1e-300,\n    2.2250738585072014e-308, 2.2250738585072009e-308,\n    1.7976931348623157e+308,\n    1.0/3.0, 2.0/3.0,\n    123456789.123456789,\n    9007199254740992.0,\n    9007199254740993.0,\n    0.0000000000000001,\n    1.7976931348623157e+308,\n]\n\nfor v in vals:\n    bits = struct.unpack('Q', struct.pack('d', v))[0]\n    r = repr(v)\n    s = str(v)\n    rt = float(r)\n    rt_bits = struct.unpack('Q', struct.pack('d', rt))[0]\n    print(f\"{bits:#018x} repr={r!r} str={s!r} roundtrip={'OK' if bits == rt_bits else 'FAIL'}\")","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":24,"totalLines":24,"truncated":false}},"title":"scratch_float_py.py","time":{"start":1788468793863,"end":1788468793871}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The board.yaml in origin/main has the float-format-research row with a full description. The current worktree is behind origin/main by 47 commits. But the brief says \"see plans/board.yaml, id float-format-research\" — that row is in origin/main's board.yaml, not in the current worktree's board.yaml. So I should treat the origin/main board row as the source for the task description. The brief already summarizes it. Also the brief says the float-build-python lane has an uncommitted diff plus scratch probe files. Let me read those files in the issue-float-build-python lane worktree.\n\n Also, I need to read the landed JS float-build implementation as reference. Let me find where the JS Float backend landed (0c29911,f22a806).\n\n\n\nLet me look at:\n1. The float-build-python lane worktree probes (~/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python)\n2. The landed JS float-build implementation (0c29911)\n3. The ADR 0007\n4. The existing scratch files in this worktree (scratch_float_go/, scratch_float_py.py）\n\nAlso let me check the float-format-research row's full text (from origin/main board.yaml) — I have the title from the grep. The brief in my task matches it. Good.\n\n\n\nLet me read the scratch files first and the python lane probes.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0690c1205001j7r4f5ix9CsWaD","sessionID":"ses_f96f44813ffeMjSGBHDZ7e2mUe","messageID":"msg_0690c0568001bDbSgmjiBiDhOB"}}
